    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d690">

                <pb facs="0737" n="479" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg479"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/1364</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at London</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 592]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 9, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 20.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s cabled
                    instruction of June 28 and my reply of June 29,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d690-f1"/>
                    I have the honor to call particular attention to my monthly trade report which
                    is annexed hereto, in triplicate. In this report will be found: (1) Some very
                    interesting figures showing the great increase in exports from this country in
                    certain lines;<anchor n="2" xml:id="d690-f2"/> and (2) a full list of the ships
                    detained at Kirkwall from March 11 to June 17, together with the period of
                    detention in each case.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d690-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert P. Skinner</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d690-a1.xml" xpointer="d690-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d690-f1" n="1" xml:id="d690-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg455">p. 455</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d690-f2" n="2" xml:id="d690-f2-content">
                <p>Only the introductory paragraphs of the report are here printed. The statistical
                    portions of part (1) are printed, in rearranged order and under the erroneous
                    date of June 15, in <hi rendition="#italic">Commerce Reports</hi> (pub. by
                    Department of Commerce), 1915, No. 180, vol. 3, p. 572.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d690-f3" n="3" xml:id="d690-f3-content">
                <p>See <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg594">p. 594</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
